## What OfferChaser changed

OfferChaser is not an independent implementation. It started from `get_jobs` and was substantially rewritten:

- retained and reworked the BOSS 直聘 delivery flow;
- removed multi-platform support;
- replaced package names and reworked the management console;
- added local rules, strict AI JSON validation, fail-closed send confirmation, session identity checks, per-day quota reservations, audit ledgers, manual-review queues, templates, and insights;
- removed inherited personal blacklist entries, personal greeting / AI prompt defaults, and other upstream author-specific configuration from the bundled defaults.

## Authorship

Most of what is in OfferChaser is new work by the maintainer: of 167 classes, 118 are
additions. That layer covers the rule engine, strict-JSON AI matching and validation,
session identity checks, per-day quota reservation, the delivery ledger, the
manual-review queue, follow-up plans, profile templates, insights, job-post analysis,
and local session security. Copyright in those additions belongs to the maintainer:
Copyright (c) 2026 Yhmx6.

The base came from upstream `get_jobs`: 49 of its 88 top-level classes are still here,
with paths and class names unchanged and only the package renamed (`com.getjobs` →
`com.offerchaser`). `Boss` has grown from a single 1858-line file into a class with 10
inner types; `BossJobDataEntity` keeps upstream's 24 fields and adds 3. The 39 classes
that are gone were all platform-specific (51job / 猎聘 / 智联), plus `Bot`, `Platform`,
and the original entry point.

